      "id": "thm-of-square-roots",
      "disposition": "proof-only clarification proposed",
      "evidence": "Review alleges missing Archimedean premise, but finite ordered-field construction suffices: half the smaller of the two positive bounds is positive and strictly below both. Proposal explicitly selects these two branches in4.1/4.2. No Archimedean axiom, dependency or Statement change is needed. All square-root existence/uniqueness and positive-square claims retained."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-independent-fair-bit-streams-produce-uniforms",
      "disposition": "proof-only repair proposed",
      "evidence": "Proof3.1 now derives coordinate slabs from lower rectangles, generates rational half-open boxes in the cube, invokes their actual Borel-generator supplier, and derives independence through the actual rectangle criterion. Definitions/statements unchanged; CC/DC hypotheses retained."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-box-muller-product-density-and-radius-moment",
      "disposition": "proof-only repair proposed",
      "evidence": "Facts F4 now states sigma-algebra definition plus actual rectangle criterion. Proof2.1 integrates indicator_A indicator_B times phi(x)phi(y) by Tonelli and identifies each marginal by full-coordinate sets, then invokes criterion. Gaussian density/radial tail/moment unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "alg-finite-categorical-inverse-cdf",
      "disposition": "Definition clarification proposed",
      "evidence": "Explicit bounds L=1,H=r, j=floor((L+H)/2), non-strict <= branch, update, and stopping instruction. Ideal [0,1] input is totalized by zero->1, a null-event assignment; positive input outcome unchanged. Comparison/termination proof moved to existing categorical theorem with invariant and halving argument."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-finite-categorical-midpoint-count-bound",
      "disposition": "consumer and property repair proposed",
      "evidence": "Fact F2 matches >= threshold convention. Proof1.1 excludes null ideal zero event; midpoint threshold counts unchanged. Added proof3.1 shows least-index invariant/termination and ceil(log2r) cumulative-array comparisons, including r=1. All original ideal/grid probability claims retained."
    },
    {
      "id": "alg-certified-bracketed-cdf-inversion",
      "disposition": "Definition budget correction proposed",
      "evidence": "Requires N+2 evaluations and stores both endpoint evaluations before N midpoint queries. Uniform-continuity existence and cost are moved into existing proved inverse-error result; failures remain inconclusive/tail-unresolved. No spatial/global guarantee expanded."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-certified-bracketed-inverse-error",
      "disposition": "consumer and property repair proposed",
      "evidence": "Statement records successful N+2 evaluations and existence of finite modulus depth; proof1.1 derives both. Input A1 already adopts algorithm budget. Proof1.2 lower->upper half corrected to match F(mid)<=u branch and greatest admissible left endpoint. Spatial/dK/tail hypotheses and claims unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-rational-bernoulli-rejection-law-and-cost",
      "disposition": "proof supplier clarification proposed",
      "evidence": "Adds explicit geometric-series Fact F4 and invocation at0<=r<1/2 for expected attempts. No probability or resource claim altered."
    },
    {
      "id": "alg-box-muller-finite-bit-transform",
      "disposition": "Definition/property separation proposed",
      "evidence": "b,p0,pmax, exponent limits and series/split integer types explicit: log/root series N>=1, phase series J>=1, only split B>=0 permits zero, exactly matching actual supplier Definitions. Operational q/log/root/phase branches and certificate output preserved. Mathematical eta_r/resource assertion moved to existing theorem; no uncertified root computation added."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-box-muller-finite-bit-coupling-error",
      "disposition": "consumer proof repair proposed",
      "evidence": "Adds direct derivative/MVT and root facts. Proof1.1 derives square-root H\u00f6lder inequality by difference of squares. Proof2.1 derives |q-rb\u00b2|<=2eta_log, |rhat-sqrt(q)|<=eta_s and hence |rhat-rb|<=sqrt(2eta_log)+eta_s from actual output certificates. Statement/proof4.1 records exact2b random bits and3 top-level evaluator calls, without claiming3 internal evaluations. All-input fixed-configuration success condition and original BL/W1/TV bounds preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "ex-box-muller-finite-midpoint-tail",
      "disposition": "proof-only repair proposed",
      "evidence": "Explicit order argument uses increasing real log then nonnegative square comparison to show radius nonincreasing. Cutoff/tail values preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "ex-box-muller-zero-endpoint",
      "disposition": "supplier/use clarification proposed",
      "evidence": "Fact F3 explicitly links exact radius formula to actual Box\u2013Muller density supplier and tags its zero-endpoint use. Raw/midpoint/null-ideal distinctions unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "ex-inverse-cdf-near-zero-density",
      "disposition": "proof-only repair proposed",
      "evidence": "Fact F1 gives defining nonnegative root properties. Proof1.1 establishes positivity and upper bound1 by squares;2.1 makes unbounded ratio comparison explicit. No inverse/density claim changed."
